<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  Minimal entitlement set for sideloading with a FREE Apple ID
	  ("Personal Team"). Deliberately empty.

	  A free provisioning profile cannot grant App Groups, Push, HealthKit,
	  Hotspot Configuration, Wi-Fi info, Associated Domains or Sign in with
	  Apple. Requesting them fails signing, and Sideloadly's stripping is not
	  guaranteed to cover every combination. An empty dict asks for nothing, so
	  any provisioning profile satisfies it.

	  None of them are needed to test what this fork exists to test:
	    background audio         : UIBackgroundModes in Info.plist, not an entitlement
	    on-device transcription  : Apple frameworks, no entitlement
	    microphone / Bluetooth   : Info.plist usage strings only

	  What is lost in this build:
	    battery widget and watch app  (already stripped as nested bundles)
	    push notifications
	    Sign in with Apple (Google web OAuth still works)
	    Live Activity / Siri bridges that read the shared App Group

	  codemagic fork yaml copies this over RunnerRelease-prod.entitlements before
	  building, so the committed upstream file stays intact.

	  No DEVELOPMENT_TEAM placeholder on purpose: CI builds with codesigning
	  disabled, where that variable is empty, and an empty expansion inside an
	  entitlement value can produce a malformed plist.
	-->
</dict>
</plist>